<% marketing_head(@page, type: "AboutPage") %>

<section class="lp-page-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div>
    <h1 id="about-title">Why Flockwork exists.</h1>
    <p>Churches do practical work for one another every week. Flockwork exists to make that work easier to organize and simpler to share.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section lp-about" aria-labelledby="body-title">
  <div class="lp-about-copy">
    <h2 id="body-title">Every part doing its work.</h2>
    <p>Ephesians 4 describes a church as a body: joined and held together, every part doing its work, building itself up in love. A meal train is that. So is a workday, a retreat, or the Tuesday someone drives dinner across town.</p>
    <p>That work often stalls in the logistics. A spreadsheet goes missing. A text thread loses a name. One person keeps every detail in their head. Flockwork keeps the project together, so leaders can organize it sooner and more people can take part.</p>
    <p>Flockwork is made by Outpost Labs LLC in Tennessee. It was built during the AI for Church hackathon window.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<figure class="lp-photo">
  <%= image_tag "marketing/photos/#{@page.photo}.webp", width: 1152, height: 768, loading: "lazy", alt: "A neighbor delivering a bag of food to new parents at their front door" %>
</figure>

<%= render "landing/close" %>
